  "notes": "Composed of {演|えん} (perform) + {奏|そう} (play music). Takes を for the instrument or piece: ピアノを{演奏|えんそう}する. The noun form {演奏|えんそう} is extremely common in music contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {生演奏|なまえんそう}: live performance\n- {独奏|どくそう}: solo performance\n- {合奏|がっそう}: ensemble, group performance\n- {演奏会|えんそうかい}: concert, recital\n- {演奏者|えんそうしゃ}: performer, musician\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {弾|ひ}く: to play (piano, guitar, strings) — casual, everyday word\n- {吹|ふ}く: to play (wind instruments) — specifically for blowing instruments\n- {叩|たた}く: to play (drums, percussion) — specifically for striking\n- {演奏|えんそう}する: more formal, encompasses all instruments and performance contexts",
